  <name>Cyclone Pad Config</name>
  <summary>Configure the GameSir Cyclone 2 controller</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.miguelsanzbr">
    <name>Miguel Sanz</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>Cyclone Pad Config sets up the GameSir Cyclone 2 controller on Linux, without the vendor's Windows software. It talks to the controller directly, through the 2.4G dongle or the USB cable, and saves every change on the controller itself.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Four profiles: switch, rename, reset to the defaults</li>
      <li>Button remapping, including the L4/R4 back buttons, turbo and toggle</li>
      <li>Stick and trigger dead zones, hair trigger, motor strength and gyro</li>
      <li>Lighting editor: animations, frames, colours per zone, brightness and speed</li>
      <li>Live view of the pressed buttons, sticks and analog triggers, with the battery level</li>
      <li>Backup and restore of every profile and the lighting</li>
      <li>English, French and Brazilian Portuguese interface</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The device is reached through its hidraw node, which needs a udev rule installed once on the host system. The
      project page explains it and ships an installer script.</p>
    <p>This is an independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by GameSir. The protocol was
      reverse-engineered for interoperability.</p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.miguelsanzbr.gamesir-cyclone2-linux.desktop</launchable>
